      "nets": ["Net-(Q1-G)", "+5V", "USBC_VBUS_IN"],
      "observed": "Q1 is the P-channel MOSFET controlled by LTC4412 U6, but Q1.2 (source) is on +5V and Q1.3 (drain) is on USBC_VBUS_IN. U6.1 (VIN) is on USBC_VBUS_IN while U6.6 (SENSE) is on +5V.",
      "expected": "For the documented USB-input-to-5V ideal-diode path, Q1's source should be on the LTC4412 input side (USBC_VBUS_IN) and its drain on the sensed output side (+5V), matching U6's VIN and SENSE connections.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V ... Q1.2(S,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "USBC_VBUS_IN ... Q1.3(D,passive) ... U6.1(VIN,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V ... U6.6(SENSE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(Q1-G) : Q1.1(G,input) U6.5(GATE,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "USB power-path controller intended to OR/protect a USB power input"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "LTC4412 controller and p-ch mosfet. need reverse current protection mostly"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MOSFET is oriented opposite to the LTC4412 VIN-to-SENSE power path. This can prevent the controller from properly enhancing Q1 for USB input power, leaving the path dependent on the body diode or otherwise impairing USB power transfer and reverse-current protection.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Q1's source and drain are reversed relative to the LTC4412's USB-input and +5V-sense connections. This conflicts with the specified ideal-diode USB power path and is likely to impair its operation."
}

